cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LiteDIC in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "LiteDIC: a toolbox-free, CPU-only subpixel digital image correlation engine in MATLAB"
abstract: >-
  LiteDIC is a self-contained two-dimensional digital image correlation engine
  written in base MATLAB, with no compiled components and no mandatory toolboxes.
  It combines the ZNSSD correlation criterion, subpixel registration by the
  inverse-compositional Gauss-Newton method with a first-order shape function,
  spline intensity interpolation, reliability-guided propagation with multi-seed
  restart, and strain computation by pointwise least squares with a strain window
  defined in pixels.
type: software
